    "intro_html":  "Meatloaf gets mocked, and meatloaf does not care. It is one of the few dinners that actually improves after a night in the fridge, and it slices to weight better than almost anything else you can cook. This one is turkey, bound with egg and bread crumbs, glazed with ketchup and barbecue sauce, served over rice. Each serving comes to {{cal}} calories with \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost), and a genuinely cheap plate.",
